[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3566728490","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113045#issuecomment-3566728490","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113045","id":3566728490,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Ul_Uq","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-22T13:48:46Z","updated_at":"2025-11-22T13:48:46Z","body":"Static variables can't be used as types, only constants. This is likely a bug in the analyzer, it should produce a compile time error.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3566728490/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3566740864","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113045#issuecomment-3566740864","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113045","id":3566740864,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7UmCWA","user":{"login":"jinyangcruise","id":42859362,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyODU5MzYy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42859362?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise","html_url":"https://github.com/jinyangcruise","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-22T14:07:52Z","updated_at":"2025-11-22T14:07:52Z","body":"I think I have seen some addons using this way to achieve some sort of namespace.\n\nAlso, these codes are valid now:\n```\nextends Node2D\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tvar conf = get_conf()\n\tconf.test()\n\t\n\tprintt(\"conf is item\", conf is UserDef.Item) # True.\n\t\nfunc get_conf() -> UserDef.Item:\n\treturn UserDef.Item.new()\n\n```\nWhich means we can use static variable as return type of Callable and we can use `is` to check type.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3566740864/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3566748375","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113045#issuecomment-3566748375","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113045","id":3566748375,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7UmELX","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-22T14:14:58Z","updated_at":"2025-11-22T14:14:58Z","body":"> Which means we can use static variable as return type of Callable and we can use `is` to check type.\n\nIf this happens to work in some places, it wasn't intentional. The [documentation](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/scripting/gdscript/static_typing.html#what-can-be-a-type-hint) lists what can be type hints. Static variables, like non-static ones, cannot be used as type hints since their values ​​are strictly speaking unknown at compile time and can change at runtime.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3566748375/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3566749675","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113045#issuecomment-3566749675","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113045","id":3566749675,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7UmEfr","user":{"login":"jinyangcruise","id":42859362,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyODU5MzYy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42859362?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise","html_url":"https://github.com/jinyangcruise","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-22T14:17:00Z","updated_at":"2025-11-22T14:17:00Z","body":"This also works:\n```\nextends Node2D\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tvar conf = get_conf()\n\tconf.test()\n\t\n\tprintt(\"conf is item\", conf is UserDef.Item)\n\t\n\tvar item_class = load(\"res://item.gd\")\n\tprintt(\"conf is instance of item\", is_instance_of(conf, item_class))\n\t\nfunc get_conf() -> UserDef.Item:\n\treturn UserDef.Item.new()\n```\nTypes can even be stored in temporary variables. All these signs indicate that a variable can be a type. We are already used to this, aren't we?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3566749675/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3566752891","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113045#issuecomment-3566752891","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113045","id":3566752891,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7UmFR7","user":{"login":"jinyangcruise","id":42859362,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyODU5MzYy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42859362?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise","html_url":"https://github.com/jinyangcruise","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-22T14:21:41Z","updated_at":"2025-11-22T14:21:41Z","body":"```\nextends Node2D\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tvar item_class = load(\"res://item.gd\")\n\tprintt(item_class.new()) # This works\n```\nThere are plenty of using cases. Even if this is a bug, I don't think it should be fixed.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3566752891/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3566754733","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113045#issuecomment-3566754733","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113045","id":3566754733,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7UmFut","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-22T14:24:28Z","updated_at":"2025-11-22T14:24:28Z","body":"`is_instance_of()` was specifically designed for dynamic type checking. `new()` can also work dynamically. Type hints (what comes after `:` and `->`) and the right-hand sides of the `is` and `as` constructs must be known at compile time.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3566754733/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3566760309","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113045#issuecomment-3566760309","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113045","id":3566760309,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7UmHF1","user":{"login":"jinyangcruise","id":42859362,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyODU5MzYy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42859362?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise","html_url":"https://github.com/jinyangcruise","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinyangcruise/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-22T14:32:14Z","updated_at":"2025-11-22T14:32:14Z","body":"> `is_instance_of()` was specifically designed for dynamic type checking. `new()` can also work dynamically. Type hints (what comes after `:` and `->`) and the right-hand sides of the `is` and `as` constructs must be known at compile time.\n\nOK, got it. Are you against this use case? Which uses `const` instead of a static variable as Type. I find this works and no error occurs.\n\nuser_def.gd\n```\nextends Object\nclass_name UserDef\n\nconst Item = preload(\"res://item.gd\")\n```\n\nmain.gd\n```\nextends Node2D\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tvar conf: UserDef.Item = get_conf()\n\tconf.test()\n\t\n\tprintt(\"conf is item\", conf is UserDef.Item)\n\nfunc get_conf() -> UserDef.Item:\n\treturn UserDef.Item.new()\n```\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3566760309/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]